# Frontend Webapp Rules

## Screenshots = Layout and Functionality Only

When the user provides a screenshot of the webapp, treat it as a reference for **layout** and **functionality** only. Do **not** infer or replicate:

- Colors, color schemes, or palettes from the image
- Font families, font sizes, or typography choices

Match structure, component placement, spacing, and behavior. Do not copy visual styling (colors/fonts) from the screenshot.

## Always Use Global Styling Variables

Use the project’s global styling from `apps/web/src/styles.css`. Do not introduce hardcoded colors or fonts.

- **Colors**: Use semantic Tailwind classes that map to CSS variables: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground`, `bg-muted`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-card`, `border-border`, `bg-sidebar`, `text-sidebar-foreground`, etc. Never use arbitrary values like `bg-[#3b82f6]` or hex/oklch literals in components.
- **Typography**: Use the theme font (`font-sans` / `--font-sans`). Do not add new `font-family` values or arbitrary font names.
- **Radius**: Use theme radius utilities (`rounded-lg`, `rounded-md`, `--radius-*`) rather than arbitrary border-radius values.

Adding new one-off colors or fonts in components is not allowed; extend `styles.css` if new semantic tokens are needed.
